IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ntlsl-dates`
IMPORT `ntlsl-employee`

-- Long Service Leave Act 1981 (NT) -- worked cases for the employee's questions (ntlsl-employee.l4), the two deadline rules
-- and the date helpers. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (reprint REPL021); none was copied
-- from the encoding's output. The two worked examples the Act gives itself (s 11(4), (5)) are asserted to the dollar.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law; the facts are illustrative. Breached
-- traces are asserted through the questions (CONSIDER EVALTRACE ... WHEN FULFILLED inside), and one breach of each rule is
-- #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line.
-- Edges: 10 years and 9 (s 8(1)); 7 and 6 years (s 10(2)); 14, 15, 19 and 20 years (ss 8(3), 10(1A)); the anniversary
-- day and the day before (s 12); 2 months and a day over, from 31 August and 31 December (ss 8(7), 12(4)(e)); 12 months
-- and a day over, from 29 February (ss 11(7)(b), 12(3)); 3 periods and 4, 4 weeks and 3.9 (s 8(6)(b)); the due day and
-- the day after (s 11(6)); 3 and 6 years from 29 February (ss 14(2), 18A).
-- UNOFFICIAL COPY of NT legislation (copyright owned by the Northern Territory); see SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `is a leap year` 2024
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a leap year` 2100))
#ASSERT `the same day` 1 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `d` 30 9 2025
#ASSERT `the same day` 2 `months after` (`d` 15 11 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 1 2026
#ASSERT `the same day` 12 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the same day` 3 `years after` (`d` 15 6 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 6 2028
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 3 2025) `to` (`d` 30 4 2025) EQUALS 60

§§ `ss 6, 7 -- does the Act apply to me`

-- HYPOTHETICAL: Mia, a full-time storeworker in Darwin under a written contract, no award with long service leave.
-- Inputs: in the Territory, contract, another law, award, honorary, approved agreement, exemption.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies to me`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not apply to me: I am not employed in the Territory (s 6(1))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not apply to me: another law of the Territory, the Commonwealth or a State provides my long service leave (s 6(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not apply to me: an award that applies to me provides for long service leave (s 6(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not apply to me: I am employed in an honorary capacity (s 6(2)(c))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not apply to me: I do not work under a contract of service or apprenticeship, so I am not an employee (s 7(1))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies to me, but my long service leave is under the agreement the Minister approved (s 8(4), (5))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Act applies to me, but the Minister has exempted my employer for me because a long service leave scheme gives me benefits no less favourable (s 13)`
-- Two grounds at once: the first in s 6's order is given.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not apply to me: I am not employed in the Territory (s 6(1))`

§§ `s 12 -- continuous service`

-- Completed years: 1 January 2015 to 31 December 2024, both days counted, is 10 years; to 30 December 2024, 9.
#ASSERT `How many completed years of continuous service do I have` (`d` 1 1 2015) (`d` 31 12 2024) 0 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How many completed years of continuous service do I have` (`d` 1 1 2015) (`d` 30 12 2024) 0 EQUALS 9
-- 10 days that do not count move the start to 11 January 2015: 10 years at 10 January 2025, 9 at 9 January 2025.
#ASSERT `How many completed years of continuous service do I have` (`d` 1 1 2015) (`d` 10 1 2025) 10 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How many completed years of continuous service do I have` (`d` 1 1 2015) (`d` 9 1 2025) 10 EQUALS 9
-- From 29 February 2016: the 10th year is complete at the end of 28 February 2026 (fork F2), not at 27 February.
#ASSERT `How many completed years of continuous service do I have` (`d` 29 2 2016) (`d` 28 2 2026) 0 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How many completed years of continuous service do I have` (`d` 29 2 2016) (`d` 27 2 2026) 0 EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `How many completed years of continuous service do I have` (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2019) 0 EQUALS 0

-- s 12(2), (4): breaks. Inputs: reason, returned under the settlement, day interrupted, day re-employed.
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my service continuous` `I served in the Reserve Forces or Citizen Forces, on national service, or in the Civil Construction Corps` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my service continuous` `my employer ended or interrupted my employment to avoid, or with the result of avoiding, an obligation under the Act` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my service continuous` `an industrial dispute` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 9 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A dispute not settled by the return: the 2-month rule of s 12(4)(e). 2 months after 1 March 2025 is 1 May 2025.
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my service continuous` `an industrial dispute` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 5 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my service continuous` `an industrial dispute` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 2 5 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my service continuous` `my employer stood me down because of a slackness of trade` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 12 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- After an apprenticeship: 12 months.
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my service continuous` `I completed my apprenticeship with the employer` FALSE (`d` 15 1 2024) (`d` 15 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my service continuous` `I completed my apprenticeship with the employer` FALSE (`d` 15 1 2024) (`d` 16 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Any other reason: 2 months. From 31 August 2025 the last day is 31 October 2025; from 31 December 2024, 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my service continuous` `another reason (including my resignation or dismissal)` FALSE (`d` 31 8 2025) (`d` 31 10 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my service continuous` `another reason (including my resignation or dismissal)` FALSE (`d` 31 8 2025) (`d` 1 11 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my service continuous` `another reason (including my resignation or dismissal)` FALSE (`d` 31 12 2024) (`d` 28 2 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my service continuous` `another reason (including my resignation or dismissal)` FALSE (`d` 31 12 2024) (`d` 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 12(2), (5): absences.
#ASSERT `Does the absence count towards my service` `leave my employer granted with pay` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the absence count towards my service` `an absence my employer brought about to avoid, or with the result of avoiding, an obligation under the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the absence count towards my service` `service in the Reserve Forces or Citizen Forces, on national service, or in the Civil Construction Corps` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the absence count towards my service` `any other absence (unpaid leave, a stand-down, an industrial dispute, or the gap before I was re-employed)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 12(3): the apprenticeship.
#ASSERT `Does my apprenticeship count` (`d` 15 1 2024) (`d` 15 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my apprenticeship count` (`d` 15 1 2024) (`d` 16 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my apprenticeship count` (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 28 2 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my apprenticeship count` (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my apprenticeship count` (`d` 15 1 2024) (`d` 16 1 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 12(6), (8): earlier employers.
#ASSERT `Does my earlier service count` `a related corporation (a subsidiary, holding or related corporation under the Corporations Act 2001), with no break between the two` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my earlier service count` `the owner of the business, or part of it, before it was transferred to my present employer, and I moved with it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my earlier service count` `another employer` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 8 -- the entitlement`

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave` 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave` 25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave` 9 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave` 9.99 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Accrued (s 8(1), (8)): 1.3 x completed years from 10, less leave taken.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave have I accrued` 10 0 EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave have I accrued` 9 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave have I accrued` 12 0 EQUALS 15.6
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave have I accrued` 12.7 0 EQUALS 15.6
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave have I accrued` 15 0 EQUALS 19.5
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave have I accrued` 12 13 EQUALS 2.6
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave have I accrued` 10 20 EQUALS 0

-- Available to take (s 8(2), (3), (8)): 13 weeks at 10 years, then 6.5 more at 15, 20 ...
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave can I take now` 10 0 EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave can I take now` 14 0 EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave can I take now` 15 0 EQUALS 19.5
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave can I take now` 19 0 EQUALS 19.5
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave can I take now` 20 0 EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave can I take now` 9 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave can I take now` 16 13 EQUALS 6.5
#ASSERT `How many weeks of long service leave can I take now` 12 13 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 8(6), (7), s 16 -- taking the leave`

#ASSERT `Can I take my leave in these periods` 1 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave in these periods` 2 4 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave in these periods` 3 4 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave in these periods` 4 4 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave in these periods` 2 3.9 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I take my leave in these periods` 2 5 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 8(7): notice on 1 March 2025; 2 months later is 1 May 2025.
#ASSERT `Was I given enough notice of my leave` (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 5 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I given enough notice of my leave` (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 30 4 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I given enough notice of my leave` (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 30 4 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- From 31 December 2024, 2 months later is 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `Was I given enough notice of my leave` (`d` 31 12 2024) (`d` 28 2 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I given enough notice of my leave` (`d` 31 12 2024) (`d` 27 2 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 16: other work during the leave.
#ASSERT `Does the Act forbid the other work during my leave` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the Act forbid the other work during my leave` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Act forbid the other work during my leave` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 10 -- when the employment ends`

-- Inputs: how it ended, completed years, weeks already taken, reached retirement age.
-- 10 years or more (s 10(1)): the credit, 1.3 a year less leave taken.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `I resigned` 12 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 15.6
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `I resigned` 10 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 13
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `I resigned` 16 13 FALSE EQUALS JUST 7.8
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer ended my employment for a reason other than serious misconduct` 11 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 14.3
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `I died` 10 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 13
-- Serious misconduct (s 10(1A)): only the completed 10-year period (10 to 14 years), then completed 5-year periods.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct` 12 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 13
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct` 14 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 13
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct` 15 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 19.5
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct` 19 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 19.5
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct` 20 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 26
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct` 12 13 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct` 16 13 FALSE EQUALS JUST 6.5
-- 7 to under 10 years (s 10(2)).
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `I resigned` 8 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `I resigned` 8 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST 10.4
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer ended my employment for a reason other than serious misconduct` 8 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 10.4
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `I left on account of illness, incapacity, or domestic or other pressing necessity that justified leaving` 7 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 9.1
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct` 7 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- Fork F8: s 10(2)(a) (retirement age) is not limited by the manner of leaving.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct` 8 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST 10.4
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer ended my employment for a reason other than serious misconduct` 9.9 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 11.7
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `my employer ended my employment for a reason other than serious misconduct` 6 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- A death between 7 and 10 years (s 10(3), finding 4).
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `I died` 9 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `I died` 9 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST 11.7
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` `I died` 5 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0

-- s 10(4): no cash in place of leave while employed.
#ASSERT `Can I be paid out instead of taking leave` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be paid out instead of taking leave` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 7, 11 -- how much`

-- The Act's own examples. s 11(4): $15 x 40 hours x 1.3 for each of 10 years = $7,800.
#ASSERT `How much must I be paid for my long service leave` 15 (LIST 40, 40, 40, 40, 40, 40, 40, 40, 40, 40) EQUALS 7800
-- s 11(5): $30 x 1.3 x (40 + 40 + 30 + 25 + 20) = $30 x 1.3 x 155 = $6,045.
#ASSERT `How much must I be paid for my long service leave` 30 (LIST 40, 40, 30, 25, 20) EQUALS 6045
#ASSERT `How much is my pay for these weeks of leave` 15 40 13 EQUALS 7800
-- $30 x 38 hours x 6.5 weeks = $7,410.
#ASSERT `How much is my pay for these weeks of leave` 30 38 6.5 EQUALS 7410

-- s 11(1) rate of pay: fixed; else $52,000 over 2,000 ordinary hours = $26.
#ASSERT `What is my rate of pay` TRUE 25.5 0 0 EQUALS JUST 25.5
#ASSERT `What is my rate of pay` FALSE 0 52000 2000 EQUALS JUST 26
#ASSERT `What is my rate of pay` FALSE 0 52000 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 11(1) hours of work per week: fixed 38; else 1,560 hours over 52 weeks = 30.
#ASSERT `What were my hours of work per week` TRUE 38 0 EQUALS 38
#ASSERT `What were my hours of work per week` FALSE 0 1560 EQUALS 30

-- s 7(2), (4): what counts as pay.
#ASSERT `Does this payment count as part of my pay` `an over-award payment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this payment count as part of my pay` `an industry, leading hand, skill or qualification allowance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this payment count as part of my pay` `a service grant` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this payment count as part of my pay` `a bonus or incentive payment usually paid with my pay` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this payment count as part of my pay` `a bonus or incentive payment not usually paid with my pay` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does this payment count as part of my pay` `free board or lodging from my employer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this payment count as part of my pay` `commission` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this payment count as part of my pay` `a district, site or climatic allowance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this payment count as part of my pay` `overtime pay or penalty rates` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this payment count as part of my pay` `another allowance` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 7(2)(c): board $15 a week, lodging $5, unless the terms fix a value.
#ASSERT `What weekly amount for board or lodging counts as pay` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `What weekly amount for board or lodging counts as pay` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `What weekly amount for board or lodging counts as pay` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `What weekly amount for board or lodging counts as pay` TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `What weekly amount for board or lodging counts as pay` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What weekly amount for board or lodging counts as pay` FALSE FALSE TRUE 50 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 11(6), (7) -- when I must be paid`

-- s 11(6): leave fixed on 1 March 2025, pay due 30 April 2025 (day 60), $5,000 owed.
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 30 4 2025) 5000 5000 (`d` 30 4 2025) (`d` 1 6 2025) EQUALS `paid in full on time`
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 30 4 2025) 5000 5000 (`d` 1 5 2025) (`d` 1 6 2025) EQUALS `paid in full, but late`
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 30 4 2025) 5000 6000 (`d` 1 4 2025) (`d` 1 6 2025) EQUALS `paid in full on time`
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 30 4 2025) 5000 5000 (`d` 28 2 2025) (`d` 1 6 2025) EQUALS `paid in full on time`
-- $4,999 is not the whole amount.
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 30 4 2025) 5000 4999 (`d` 29 4 2025) (`d` 30 4 2025) EQUALS `not yet paid in full, and not yet due`
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 30 4 2025) 5000 4999 (`d` 29 4 2025) (`d` 1 5 2025) EQUALS `not yet paid in full, and overdue`

-- s 11(7)(b): a death on 31 March 2025; the last day is 31 March 2026. From 29 February 2024, 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must my estate be paid` (`d` 31 3 2025) EQUALS `d` 31 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must my estate be paid` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `Was my estate paid on time` (`d` 31 3 2025) 20000 20000 (`d` 31 3 2026) (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `paid in full on time`
#ASSERT `Was my estate paid on time` (`d` 31 3 2025) 20000 20000 (`d` 1 4 2026) (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `paid in full, but late`
#ASSERT `Was my estate paid on time` (`d` 31 3 2025) 20000 0 (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 31 3 2026) EQUALS `not yet paid in full, and not yet due`
#ASSERT `Was my estate paid on time` (`d` 31 3 2025) 20000 0 (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `not yet paid in full, and overdue`

-- The rules themselves, on a timeline in days.
#TRACE `s 11(6) -- pay the whole of the leave before it starts` 5000 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my employer` DOES `pay my long service leave` 5000 AT 60
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 11(6) -- pay the whole of the leave before it starts` 5000 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my employer` DOES `pay my long service leave` 5000 AT 61
-- expect: BREACH by my employer (paid on day 61, after the day 60 deadline)
#TRACE `s 11(7)(b) -- pay the estate within 12 months of the death` 20000 365 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my employer` DOES `pay my personal representative` 19000 AT 100
    (WAITUNTIL 366)
-- expect: BREACH by my employer (a part payment does not count; 365 days pass)

§§ `ss 14, 17, 18, 18A -- records and enforcement`

#ASSERT `Until when must my leave records be kept` FALSE (`d` 15 6 2025) (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `d` 15 6 2028
#ASSERT `Until when must my leave records be kept` TRUE (`d` 31 3 2025) (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2030
#ASSERT `Until when must my leave records be kept` TRUE (`d` 31 3 2025) (`d` 10 9 2025) EQUALS `d` 10 9 2031

#ASSERT `Do my rights stand despite my agreement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do my rights stand despite my agreement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do my rights stand despite my agreement` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `By when can my employer be prosecuted` (`d` 10 5 2025) EQUALS `d` 10 5 2028
#ASSERT `By when can my employer be prosecuted` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `s 18(1) -- the maximum penalty in penalty units` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `s 18(1) -- the maximum imprisonment in months` EQUALS 6
